---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
const SIZES = [10, 100, 1000, 10000, 100000];
const UPDATES = [1, 10, 100, 1000];
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="A cart read by three widgets, updated several times. Pick how updates are made and see what the readers see and how many elements get copied. Costs come from a simple counting model, not from timing.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Set <b>Update style</b> to <b>Shared mutable data</b>: the three widgets show <b>3,510, 3,159, 2,842</b> for one cart, and all 3 readers see the list change. Set <b>Update style</b> to <b>Copy on every update</b>: the totals are <b>3,510, 3,510, 3,510</b> and no reader is surprised.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Items</b> to <b>10,000</b> and <b>Updates</b> to <b>100</b>. <b>Copy on every update</b> costs <b>1,000,000</b> element copies, <b>Structural sharing</b> only <b>9,600</b>, and <b>Shared mutable data</b> only <b>100</b>.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Items</b> to <b>10</b>: now <b>Copy on every update</b> costs <b>1,000</b> and <b>Structural sharing</b> costs <b>3,200</b>, so the clever structure loses on small data. The crossover is at <b>65</b> items.</li>
    <li>Look at <b>Private copy, then freeze</b>: at <b>Items</b> of 10 it costs <b>110</b> copies for 100 updates, and at 10,000 items <b>10,100</b>. It is safe because nobody sees the copy until it is finished.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg imm" data-imm>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Update style <select class="pg-in" data-style>
        <option value="0" selected>Shared mutable data</option>
        <option value="1">Copy on every update</option>
        <option value="2">Structural sharing</option>
        <option value="3">Private copy, then freeze</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Items <select class="pg-in" data-n>{SIZES.map((n) => <option value={n} selected={n === 10000}>{n.toLocaleString('en-US')}</option>)}</select></label>
      <label>Updates <select class="pg-in" data-u>{UPDATES.map((u) => <option value={u} selected={u === 100}>{u.toLocaleString('en-US')}</option>)}</select></label>
      <label>Readers holding the list <input class="pg-in" type="number" min="0" max="10" value="3" data-r /></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Element copies</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Readers surprised</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Three widgets show</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4 style="--c: var(--role-3)"><h3>Crossover</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)">
      <h3>All four styles at these settings</h3>
      <div class="imm-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Element copies for each update style"><table class="imm-table" data-table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Style</th><th scope="col">Element copies</th><th scope="col">Readers surprised</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody></tbody>
      </table></div>
      <span class="pg-note">Model: an in-place update is one write. Copying everything copies n items per update. Structural sharing copies one 32-slot node per tree level per update. A private copy copies n once, then updates in place. A real persistent structure has more overhead than this count shows, and real copies of arrays are typically cheap per element, so treat the table as the shape of the cost, not a timing.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, formatThousands } from '../playground';
  const COUPON = 90;
  const STYLES = ['Shared mutable data', 'Copy on every update', 'Structural sharing', 'Private copy, then freeze'];
  const sum = (a: number[]) => a.reduce((x, y) => x + y, 0);
  const previewImpure = (cart: number[]) => { for (let i = 0; i < cart.length; i++) cart[i] = Math.floor((cart[i] * COUPON) / 100); return sum(cart); };
  const previewPure = (cart: number[]) => sum(cart.map((p) => Math.floor((p * COUPON) / 100)));
  function treeDepth(n: number): number {
    let levels = 1, capacity = 32;
    while (capacity < n) { capacity *= 32; levels++; }
    return levels;
  }
  function copies(style: number, n: number, u: number): number {
    if (style === 0) return u;
    if (style === 1) return u * n;
    if (style === 2) return u * treeDepth(n) * 32;
    return n + u;
  }
  const surprised = (style: number, r: number, u: number) => (style === 0 && u > 0 ? r : 0);
  function widgets(style: number): number[] {
    const cart = [1000, 2500, 400];
    return [0, 1, 2].map(() => (style === 0 ? previewImpure(cart) : previewPure(cart)));
  }
  let crossover = 1;
  while (!(treeDepth(crossover) * 32 < crossover)) crossover++;

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-imm]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const tbody = q('[data-table] tbody');
    const box = (n: number, good: boolean) => q<HTMLElement>(`[data-b${n}]`).style.setProperty('--c', good ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
    const set = (n: number, out: string, note: string) => { q(`[data-o${n}]`).textContent = out; q(`[data-n${n}]`).textContent = note; };
    function draw() {
      const style = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-style]').value);
      const n = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-n]').value);
      const u = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-u]').value);
      const r = Math.max(0, Math.min(10, Math.floor(Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-r]').value) || 0)));
      const c = copies(style, n, u);
      set(1, formatThousands(c), `${STYLES[style]}: ${formatThousands(u)} updates of ${formatThousands(n)} items`);
      box(1, c <= u * 100);
      const s = surprised(style, r, u);
      set(2, `${s} of ${r}`, s === 0 ? 'every reader keeps the version it was given' : 'readers see the list change under them');
      box(2, s === 0);
      const w = widgets(style);
      set(3, w.map(formatThousands).join(', '), style === 0 ? 'each call applies the coupon to the cart again' : 'the same cart gives the same total every time');
      box(3, w[0] === w[1] && w[1] === w[2]);
      set(4, formatThousands(crossover), `structural sharing beats copying everything from this many items; at ${formatThousands(n)} items it ${treeDepth(n) * 32 < n ? 'wins' : 'loses'}`);
      tbody.textContent = '';
      STYLES.forEach((name, i) => {
        const tr = document.createElement('tr');
        if (i === style) tr.className = 'sel';
        [name, formatThousands(copies(i, n, u)), `${surprised(i, r, u)} of ${r}`].forEach((text, k) => {
          const cell = document.createElement(k === 0 ? 'th' : 'td'); if (k === 0) cell.setAttribute('scope', 'row'); cell.textContent = text; tr.appendChild(cell);
        });
        tbody.appendChild(tr);
      });
    }
    root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    root.addEventListener('input', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .imm-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .playground .imm-table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: .85rem; }
  .playground .imm-table th, .playground .imm-table td { padding: 5px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); text-align: left; }
  .playground .imm-table tr.sel { background: var(--accent-soft); font-weight: 600; }
</style>
